# Upload trimming for the ARQ worker service ONLY.
#
# The worker is the one service deployed from the REPO ROOT (see railway.toml for why its
# config file cannot live in backend/). Without this file every `railway up` from the root
# would upload the frontend, the landing site, the docs and the load tests -- none of which
# backend/Dockerfile.worker copies into the image.
#
# This file is never consulted by the API or frontend deploys: those run
# `cd backend|frontend && railway up . --path-as-root`, so the repo root is not their
# archive root and this file is not in their upload.
#
# `railway up` already honors .gitignore, so node_modules/.venv/build output need no entry.

frontend/
landing/
load-tests/
docs/
nginx/
supabase/
signature/
e2e/
.github/
.claude/
